Third-party material this project uses or ships

Acoustic model (downloaded at first use, not in this repository)
  anyspeech/zipa-small-crctc-500k, CC BY 4.0. Zhu et al., "ZIPA: A family of efficient models for
  multilingual phone recognition", github.com/lingjzhu/zipa. The "-ns-" ZIPA variants are
  CC BY-NC-SA and are not used.

Shipped data files with their own licenses (pronunciada/data/lex; per-file list in LICENSE.txt there)
  en        CMUdict, BSD-2-Clause-style, (C) Carnegie Mellon University
  de, fr    ipa-dict, MIT;  es: word list from ipa-dict (MIT), pronunciations by rule
  it, pt, ru  derived from WikiPron / Wiktionary: CC BY-SA, attribution "Wiktionary
            contributors". These files (it.tsv.gz, it_lts.tsv.gz, pt.tsv.gz, ru.tsv.gz,
            ru_stress.tsv.gz) stay under CC BY-SA when redistributed; the Apache license of the
            code does not apply to them. The output adapters pronunciada/data/adapters/it.npz,
            pt.npz and ru.npz, trained towards references built from these files, are treated as
            share-alike adaptations as well (CC BY-SA 4.0, same attribution).
  ru_stress_extra.tsv.gz  stress marks (and restored ё) for 14 040 Russian word forms missing from
            ru.tsv.gz, derived offline with silero-stress 1.5 (MIT, github.com/snakers4/silero-stress)
            from FLEURS-ru train/validation and Common Voice ru (CC0) sentence text
            (bench/calib/ru_stress_lex.py). silero-stress is not a runtime dependency.

Runtime text packages (optional extras, installed separately)
  pypinyin (MIT), jieba (MIT), opencc-python-reimplemented (Apache-2.0), pyopenjtalk-plus (MIT,
  bundles Open JTalk / NAIST-jdic under BSD licenses). pyopenjtalk-plus also installs
  sudachipy + sudachidict-core (Apache-2.0), which Pronunciada does not use.

Models trained for this project (pronunciada/data; details per file in docs/LICENSING.md)
  Output adapters, stress models, attribute heads, length model: FLEURS (Google, CC BY 4.0).
  Sound / word / sentence calibrators: speechocean762 train (CC BY 4.0 on OpenSLR); the word
  model also uses FLEURS validation planted errors. Nothing shipped is fitted on, or selected
  with, L2-ARCTIC or EpaDB (the word model was re-fitted without them on 2026-11-17;
  results/licence_refit.md).
  Korean sound-identity head (data/coach/ko_identity.npz): FLEURS ko train and Zeroth-Korean
  train (Zeroth project, openslr.org/40, CC BY 4.0; read via the Hugging Face copy kresnik/zeroth_korean).
  Mandarin defaults, coaching models: OMPAL dev (CC BY 4.0), Common Voice (CC0).
  Round-19 sound-identity heads and word rules (de, es, pt, ru, zh, ja) and the Japanese length
  model: FLEURS and Common Voice 22.0 (CC0). English sentence heads (sentence_r19, seqhead_en):
  speechocean762 train.
  Some files were trained on labels taken from references built partly from the it / pt / ru
  CC BY-SA lexicons (data/coach/identity/pt.npz and ru.npz, data/prosody/stress_v3.onnx,
  data/coach/attr_heads.npz); whether they are treated as share-alike like the adapters is an
  open question in docs/LICENSING.md. Per-file list: pronunciada/data/LICENSES_SHIPPED.json.
  Mandarin tone models: AISHELL-3 (OpenSLR SLR93) and AISHELL-1 (OpenSLR SLR33), both Apache
  License 2.0 (200 of the 300 AISHELL-1 speakers were fetched from a community mirror that
  re-hosts the same corpus), Common Voice zh-TW (CC0), FLEURS zh train.

Benchmark data (not shipped; nothing shipped was fitted or selected on L2-ARCTIC or EpaDB)
  L2-ARCTIC (CC BY-NC 4.0), EpaDB, Microsoft Azure Pronunciation Assessment responses
  (cached outside the repository; only aggregate statistics are in results/).
  OMPAL corpus (CC BY 4.0), github.com/phantomhsieh/OMPAL-corpus: Hsieh et al., "OMPAL: Bridging
  Speech and Learning with an Open-Source Mandarin Pronunciation Assessment Corpus for Global
  Learners", Interspeech 2025, doi:10.21437/Interspeech.2025-983 (test half: benchmark; dev half:
  tuning, see above).
  praat-parselmouth (GPL-3.0) is used offline to cross-check the pitch tracker only.

Sample recordings (site/samples/, the only benchmark audio in the repository)
  Nine CC BY 4.0 test-split clips from speechocean762, FLEURS and OMPAL; sources and citations in
  site/samples/ATTRIBUTION.md.
